    "seasonOutlook": "Tyson was selected by the Saints with the No. 8 overall pick of April's draft. He is a versatile receiver with decent size who led this rookie class with a 35% target share during the nine weeks he was active in 2025. Injuries cost him time during all four collegiate seasons, but he still managed a 158-2,282-22 receiving line in 33 games, posting a strong 2.73 YPRR along the way (third best in this class). Tyson will begin his career playing second fiddle to Chris Olave, but with little additional target competition, the rookie has a path to a substantial role in an ascending offense led by second-year QB Tyler Shough. Tyson can be valued as a WR3/flex.",
