    "seasonOutlook": "Kirk signed with the 49ers after spending his first eight seasons with Arizona, Jacksonville and Houston. The 2018 second-round pick peaked with a 12th-place finish in fantasy points in 2022, but that marks his only career top-25 finish and he's been way off the fantasy radar the last two seasons, partially due to injury woes (13 missed games). Kirk doesn't necessarily have a clear path to consistent targets, but with only 33-year-old Mike Evans and unproven Ricky Pearsall clearly ahead of him on the depth chart (and with George Kittle recovering from a torn Achilles), there's at least a chance he sees a fair share of Brock Purdy's targets in one of the league's most efficient offenses. The 29-year-old isn't the worst late flier in very deep leagues.",
