    "seasonOutlook": "Brazzell was selected by the Panthers in the third round of April's draft. Brazzell is a tall, perimeter receiver with a big wingspan who will do most of his damage down field (career 14.2 aDOT at Tennessee) and doesn't offer much after the catch (3.6 RAC was worst in this rookie WR class). He has good speed (4.37 40-yard dash) and may settle in as a boom/bust low-volume, splash-play fantasy option. He'll begin his career battling with Jalen Coker and Xavier Legette for work behind No. 1 receiver Tetairoa McMillan. Brazzell is barely worth late-round consideration, but makes for a fine dynasty stash.",
